&lt;p&gt;We’re waving goodbye to the complicated and confusing ways of traditional banking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After starting as a prepaid card, our product offering has grown a lot in the last 10 years in the UK. As well as&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/personal&quot;&gt;personal&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/business-banking&quot;&gt;business&lt;/a&gt; bank accounts, we offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/joint-account&quot;&gt;joint accounts&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/16-17&quot;&gt;accounts for 16-17 year olds&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/current-account/under-16s&quot;&gt;free kids account&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/flex&quot;&gt;credit cards&lt;/a&gt; in the UK, with more exciting things to come beyond. Our UK customers can also &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/savings&quot;&gt;save&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/investments&quot;&gt;invest &lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/pensions&quot;&gt;combine their pensions&lt;/a&gt; with us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our hot coral cards and get-paid-early feature, combined with financial education on social media and our award winning customer service, we have a long history of creating magical moments for our customers!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re not about selling products - we want to solve problems and change lives through Monzo ❤️&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📍London / Distributed (UK) | 💰 £86,100 - £101,300 (depending on experience) ➕ incentive awards tied to your performance |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers#benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tDAT6VxoqQM&quot;&gt;Hear from the team&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⭐ About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strategic, commercially minded, and data-driven &lt;strong&gt;Senior Strategy and Operations Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, who will be an individual contributor and help shape the future of Payments at Monzo. You’ll play a critical role in supporting the GM of Payments and the leadership team to define, measure, and drive our strategy - balancing long-term vision with the realities of day-to-day delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership, high-impact role, ideal for someone who thrives on solving complex problems, is fuelled by strategic thinking, and enjoys using data to bring clarity to ambiguity. You’ll move seamlessly between blue-sky thinking and tactical execution - one day modelling the impact of a new product bet, the next helping optimise how we run the collective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll bring a birds-eye view across Payments’s portfolio - ensuring our goals, investments, and initiatives line up coherently with each other and with Monzo’s broader mission. And you’ll be the connective tissue that keeps us operating effectively: tracking performance, surfacing insights, and making sure we’re focused on what really matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔑 You’ll play a key role by…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving strategic clarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Supporting the GM of Payments and leadership team in defining, tracking, and evolving Payments’s strategic direction to align with Monzo’s wider mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively dive into large, complex datasets to uncover insights, diagnose operational challenges, and independently design and implement scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translating data into action:&lt;/strong&gt; Building and maintaining data-informed views of performance across products, squads, and initiatives; using insights to inform priorities and trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Partnering closely with Product, Engineering, Data and Design teams to bridge the gap between ideas and strategic business execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owning business performance rhythm:&lt;/strong&gt; Leading monthly business reviews, reporting, and governance materials to keep the collective aligned and accountable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shaping new opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Scoping new bets through market sizing, commercial modelling, partnerships evaluation, and budget/forecast analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Making the org more effective:&lt;/strong&gt; Optimising how we balance KTLO, BAU, and growth work; supporting resourcing and squad setup decisions across the collective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connecting the dots:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensuring consistent communication and alignment across Payment squads, and with other Monzo collectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale &amp;amp; Geographic Expansion:&lt;/strong&gt; Playing a pivotal role in scaling our lending book and supporting launch operations as we expand our Borrowing products into new geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bringing teams together:&lt;/strong&gt; Leading Payments All Hands, goals processes, and strategic forums that ensure cohesion and momentum across the collective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 We’d love to hear from you if you have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; You have a deeply strategic mind, capable of seeing the bigger picture, thinking in systems, and anticipating future trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional Problem-Solving Skills: &lt;/strong&gt;Your “superpower” is solving complex problems with analytical rigor, commercial viability, and execution certainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability &amp;amp; Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re a self-starter who thrives in ambiguity, adept at navigating complex, rapidly evolving environments, and driven by impact and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Influencing Without Authority:&lt;/strong&gt; You have an exceptional ability to connect the dots across different parts of the business, foster collaboration, and drive alignment without authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re comfortable making trade-offs and prioritisation decisions based on data, business impact, and resource constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Rigour&lt;/strong&gt;: A strong analytical skillset with a proven track record of comfortably navigating large datasets to solve unstructured problems independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with highly technical teams such as Machine Learning and Data/Analytics Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re motivated by improving how teams work - finding ways to make organisations more efficient, scalable, and focused on what matters most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🙌 What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 £86,100 - £101,300 (depending on experience) + incentive awards tied to your performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍 We&#39;re open to distributed working within the UK, with the expectation of working from the London office on occasional basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⏰ We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, and at times that suit you and your team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 £1,000 learning budget each year to use on books, training courses and conferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏡 We will set you up to work from home; all employees are given Macbooks and for fully remote workers we will provide extra support for your work-from-home setup.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;➕ Plus lots more!&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers#benefits&quot;&gt;Read our full list of benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈 The application journey has 4 key steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phone call with Recruiter (30 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initial behavioural video call with Hiring Manager (45 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical interview (60 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem solving interview (60 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our average process takes around 3–4 weeks, but we will always work around your availability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll only close this role once we have enough applications for the next stage. Please submit your application as soon as possible to make sure you don’t miss out.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo. You can read them&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-NZ1 #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
